# Repin to a new release:
#  1. Take the asset URL from the release notes and replace the url in
#     plugin.json, in each surreal: line of examples/, topics/ and verify/, and
#     in the snippets of overview.md. Copy the examples again from the tag with
#     the sed of the "examples/" line below.
#  2. If the new `.roc-version` names another commit of the fork, update
#     `compiler` in plugin.json and link that build at roc_<compiler>/roc.
#  3. Run `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index plugins/surrealdb`, then
#     `plugin validate plugins/surrealdb --attest`.
#  4. Redo the findings of the overview, and update this file.

# The compiler is NOT a nightly. The package needs the reify fork of Roc
# (`Karakatiza666/roc`, branch reify, commit c1e6af27a29303f2e409b037aa1d4a32ebd68217
# = the package's .roc-version, based on nightly-2026-11-03-34bd006). Stock Roc
# has no `Code` type. Build it with Zig 0.17.0 (`zig build roc`, a debug build
# whose `roc version` prints debug-c1e6af27). The `compiler` of plugin.json
# names the fork in the .roc-version form, and the gates check every program of
# this plugin with roc_<compiler>/roc at the repo root, so link the build there:
#
#   mkdir roc_reify-c1e6af27a29303f2e409b037aa1d4a32ebd68217
#   ln -s <fork>/zig-out/bin/roc roc_reify-c1e6af27a29303f2e409b037aa1d4a32ebd68217/roc
#
# CI builds no fork. Run `plugin validate plugins/surrealdb --attest` locally
# after every change, and commit the BUILD-PROOF it writes. CI and the publish
# workflow check that file with `plugin validate --offline --proof`.
compiler reify-c1e6af27a29303f2e409b037aa1d4a32ebd68217

BUILD-PROOF <- written by `plugin validate --attest` (see above), not upstream's
index.json  <- the bundle's modules (src/Surreal.roc and the modules it imports),
               parsed by `roc-syntax-mcp plugin index`. Public: Surreal only
               (src/main.roc exposes nothing else); the rest are host tier. No
               source is vendored
examples/   <- monitoring.roc, search.roc, client.roc, watch.roc and server.roc
               of the repo's examples/, repinned with two edits per file:
               `surreal: "../src/main.roc"` is the url above (the sed
               `s#"\.\./src/main\.roc"#"<url>"#`), and the file gains one `##`
               title line above everything, which `list_roc_index(kind:
               "examples")` prints. Nothing else differs
topics/     <- this package's own: programs written against this pin and
               declared in plugin.json. surreal_session and surreal_live were
               run against SurrealDB 3.3.4 (docker image
               surrealdb/surrealdb:v3.3.4, memory) with the port changed to a
               free one; the rest print SurrealQL and need no server.
overview.md <- this package's own. Each snippet is in verify/overview-snippets.roc

# What examples/ leaves out, and why:
#   main.roc  the best place to learn the query API, but `app [main!]
#             { surreal: ..., clinic: "clinic/main.roc" }` imports the sibling
#             package examples/clinic/, and the gate compiles one file at a time
#             (`examples/*.roc`, each one an app). topics/surreal_queries.roc
#             and surreal_schema.roc teach the same calls in single files
#   clinic/   the package that main.roc imports (helpers over open rows)
#   README.md of examples/ is prose for contributors

# What else the repo has and this package does not ship:
#   README.md      2500 lines. The overview and the topics give what an app
#                  author needs; the README stays the reference for the
#                  builtin table, the SurrealQL of each call and the design
#                  limits
#   tests/, scripts/, .github/, dist/, src/internal.roc  contributor material
#                  (internal.roc is a second header that exposes every module for
#                  the tests)

# Compiler findings of this pin (the overview has the ones an app author needs):
#  - `rows = read.result.map_err(Str.inspect)?` on the `result` of `Session.run!`,
#    when `rows` holds a list, stops the debug fork with "ARC: use of unbound
#    refcounted local" (post-check arc). Matching on `result` compiles.
#  - The stock nightly 2026-11-03-34bd006 rejects every builder call
#    with "missing method" and give no hint about `Code`.
#  - The warning "unconditional condition" appears when a `match` runs on a
#    value that is known at compile time (a `Try` from a top-level `prepare`);
#    the topics match inside a function to avoid it.

